    "created_at": "2026-11-22T23:14:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T23:14:21Z",
    "body": "The check is green on `main`. We did not reproduce the failure.\n\n- Command: `cargo xtask catalog --check`. A clean worktree ran it on `main` at `16dc39f06`. No commit after `16dc39f06` changes `xtask/` or `examples/catalog/`, so the result also applies to `main` at `4c0a157e1`.\n- Result: exit code 0. The line for the case is `checked 2d/drill-overfeed (refusal)`. All 14 catalog cases show `checked`. The check left no changed files.\n- The fix commit: not found. PR #3162 (merge `57a188a34`, 2026-11-22 06:52Z) added the refusal mode. It added `expect = \"refusal\"`, the case `2d/drill-overfeed` and the refusal arm in `validate_layout`. The checker asks for an `.nc` file only when a case has `expect = \"post\"`. No later commit changes this code.\n- The `fd64cc2f` commit and the head of PR #3523 (`01743ad74`) both contain `57a188a34`. Thus the tree of the report already had the refusal arm. We cannot say why the check was red in that run.\n- An existing test pins this behaviour: `catalog_check_verifies_refusal_case` in `xtask/tests/catalog.rs`.\n\nWe made no claim and no PR. If the reporter agrees, a collaborator can close this issue as already done.\n",
